WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.828 --> 00:00:16.890
do you mean, your painting is gone?"

2
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.311
Henry asked Nathan.

3
00:00:19.091 --> 00:00:19.872
"Where did it go?"

4
00:00:19.892 --> 00:00:21.593
"I don't know."

5
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:23.274
Nathan sounded upset.

6
00:00:24.195 --> 00:00:26.856
"That's what I need The Lemonade Detectives to figure out!"

7
00:00:27.877 --> 00:00:29.478
Cole handed him some lemonade.

8
00:00:29.498 --> 00:00:31.880
"Here, drink this," he said.

9
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.181
"Then tell us what happened."

10
00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:36.823
Nathan gulped down the lemonade.

11
00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:41.266
"I wanted to get a snack before the judging started," he said.

12
00:00:41.286 --> 00:00:45.529
"I left the art show for a few minutes to go to the taco stand.

13
00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:49.091
When I got back, my painting was gone!"

14
00:00:49.111 --> 00:00:51.433
"How could it just disappear?"

15
00:00:51.753 --> 00:00:52.493
Maggie asked.

16
00:00:53.314 --> 00:00:55.035
"There were all kinds of people around.

17
00:00:55.616 --> 00:00:57.137
Somebody must have seen what happened."

18
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.258
Nathan shook his head.

19
00:00:59.278 --> 00:01:01.780
"Nora wandered off a little while ago.

20
00:01:02.976 --> 00:01:04.397
My mom went to look for her.

21
00:01:05.118 --> 00:01:07.100
So they weren't there when it disappeared."

22
00:01:08.061 --> 00:01:08.901
He looked upset.

23
00:01:08.921 --> 00:01:11.383
"Will you guys take the case?"

24
00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:13.906
"Of course," Henry said.

25
00:01:13.926 --> 00:01:16.728
"Let's go take a look at the scene of the crime."

26
00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:20.651
They closed the lemonade stand and walked over to the art show.

27
00:01:23.774 --> 00:01:25.976
The spot where Nathan's painting had hung was empty.

28
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:28.057
Nathan bit his lip.

29
00:01:28.077 --> 00:01:30.720
"What do you think happened to my painting?"

30
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.281
"That's what we need to find out."

31
00:01:33.961 --> 00:01:34.902
Henry looked around.

32
00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.803
There were other paintings hanging nearby.

33
00:01:37.823 --> 00:01:42.146
"Did you ask any of the other artists if they saw anything?"

34
00:01:43.287 --> 00:01:44.067
Nathan nodded.

35
00:01:44.087 --> 00:01:46.328
"There weren't many people nearby.

36
00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:48.129
Nobody saw a thing."

37
00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:50.891
"Why would someone steal a painting?"

38
00:01:51.171 --> 00:01:51.831
Maggie wondered.

39
00:01:51.851 --> 00:01:53.833
"Wait, I know!

40
00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.153
What about Patrick?"

41
00:01:56.194 --> 00:01:56.894
Henry nodded.

42
00:01:56.914 --> 00:01:59.596
"I was about to ask the same thing.

43
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.222
Patrick seems suspicious to me."

44
00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:04.043
Cole nodded.

45
00:02:04.063 --> 00:02:08.827
"Patrick seemed mad when Owen told us what the judges said about Nathan's painting.

46
00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:12.570
Patrick might be trying to knock out the competition."

47
00:02:13.531 --> 00:02:14.772
Maggie clenched her fists.

48
00:02:15.492 --> 00:02:16.693
"Let's go talk to him!"

49
00:02:16.713 --> 00:02:20.276
"Wait." Henry turned to Nathan.

50
00:02:20.997 --> 00:02:23.879
"Has anyone else said anything about your painting?"

51
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.001
Nathan shrugged.

52
00:02:26.461 --> 00:02:27.042
"Just Mr.

53
00:02:27.062 --> 00:02:28.963
Collins." "Mr.

54
00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:30.905
Collins?" Henry was surprised.

55
00:02:31.946 --> 00:02:35.009
Mr. Collins was a barber who entered the art show every year.

56
00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:36.670
"What do you mean?"

57
00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:41.754
"He noticed my painting earlier today and seemed kind of upset," Nathan said.

58
00:02:41.774 --> 00:02:45.017
"He says it's really similar to his painting."

59
00:02:45.037 --> 00:02:47.139
"Is it similar?"

60
00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:48.120
Henry asked.

61
00:02:49.161 --> 00:02:50.022
Nathan shrugged.

62
00:02:50.042 --> 00:02:51.403
"I don't know.

63
00:02:51.423 --> 00:02:52.804
I haven't seen his painting."

64
00:02:52.824 --> 00:02:54.966
"What are we waiting for?"

65
00:02:55.206 --> 00:02:55.786
Maggie said.

66
00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:57.248
"Let's go check it out."

67
00:03:02.632 --> 00:03:04.092
It didn't take long to find Mr.

68
00:03:04.132 --> 00:03:04.993
Collins' painting.

69
00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:07.674
Cole wrinkled his nose when he saw it.

70
00:03:08.314 --> 00:03:11.355
"That doesn't look like your painting at all," he told Nathan.

71
00:03:11.375 --> 00:03:14.115
"Yeah," Maggie agreed.

72
00:03:14.135 --> 00:03:17.116
"It looks like a bunch of crazy cubes."

73
00:03:18.217 --> 00:03:20.657
A woman standing nearby heard them and looked over.

74
00:03:20.677 --> 00:03:22.838
"Are you talking about Mr.

75
00:03:22.878 --> 00:03:23.658
Collins' piece?"

76
00:03:24.018 --> 00:03:24.498
she asked.

77
00:03:24.518 --> 00:03:26.579
"It's wonderful, isn't it?

78
00:03:27.899 --> 00:03:29.900
He calls it Calico at Rest.

79
00:03:30.496 --> 00:03:32.837
He has such a way with the Cubist style!"

80
00:03:32.857 --> 00:03:36.378
"It's very nice," Henry said politely.

81
00:03:37.418 --> 00:03:38.738
Then he led his friends away.

82
00:03:38.758 --> 00:03:42.520
"I guess both paintings have calico cats.

83
00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.620
But they don't look alike."

84
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.501
"That's for sure!"

85
00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:47.601
blurted out Maggie.

86
00:03:47.621 --> 00:03:51.682
"Mr. Collins is pretty sensitive," said Cole.

87
00:03:52.322 --> 00:03:54.523
"Maybe he thinks Nathan copied his idea."

88
00:03:54.543 --> 00:03:56.504
"But I didn't!"

89
00:03:56.824 --> 00:03:57.824
Nathan protested.

90
00:03:58.888 --> 00:04:02.130
"We know you didn't copy him," Henry assured Nathan.

91
00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.192
"But Mr.

92
00:04:04.212 --> 00:04:05.213
Collins might not.

93
00:04:05.893 --> 00:04:08.475
He should probably be on our suspect list."

94
00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:10.616
"And Patrick too, right?"

95
00:04:10.837 --> 00:04:11.577
Cole asked.

96
00:04:11.597 --> 00:04:14.019
"Definitely," Henry said.

97
00:04:14.039 --> 00:04:17.361
"Nathan and Patrick are in the same age category.

98
00:04:18.242 --> 00:04:20.763
That means Patrick has a better motive than Mr.

99
00:04:20.804 --> 00:04:24.786
Collins." Maggie was biting her lip, looking worried.

100
00:04:24.806 --> 00:04:26.207
"What about Hannah?"

101
00:04:26.447 --> 00:04:26.908
she said.

102
00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:28.540
"What about her?"

103
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:29.501
Cole asked.

104
00:04:29.521 --> 00:04:33.943
"She got upset when we mentioned Nathan's painting earlier, remember?"

105
00:04:34.243 --> 00:04:34.843
Maggie said.

106
00:04:34.863 --> 00:04:37.144
"And she loves cats."

107
00:04:38.485 --> 00:04:40.125
Henry realized Maggie was right.

108
00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:44.868
"Hannah didn't seem to like the painting part of the show," he said.

109
00:04:44.888 --> 00:04:49.690
"But I'm not sure that would make her steal Nathan's painting."

110
00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.390
Cole shrugged.

111
00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.732
"We should probably talk to Hannah, just in case."

112
00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.009
"I thought of another suspect," Maggie said.

113
00:04:58.029 --> 00:05:00.969
"That woman with the big sunglasses.

114
00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.550
She seemed pretty weird."

115
00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.831
"True," Henry said.

116
00:05:05.851 --> 00:05:09.012
"But why would she steal Nathan's painting?

117
00:05:10.092 --> 00:05:11.472
We don't even know who she is."

118
00:05:11.492 --> 00:05:14.453
"Maybe she's an international art thief."

119
00:05:14.693 --> 00:05:15.854
Maggie sounded excited.

120
00:05:15.874 --> 00:05:20.435
"She could be lurking around the show, looking for valuable paintings to steal!"

121
00:05:22.475 --> 00:05:24.596
Henry traded a look with Cole and Nathan.

122
00:05:25.328 --> 00:05:27.670
Maggie liked to exaggerate things sometimes.

123
00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:31.632
"I doubt the woman is a thief," Henry told Maggie.

124
00:05:31.652 --> 00:05:34.614
"But she was acting pretty weird.

125
00:05:35.354 --> 00:05:37.576
I guess we can put her on the list of suspects."

126
00:05:38.676 --> 00:05:39.917
Nathan looked impatient.

127
00:05:40.617 --> 00:05:41.958
"So what do we do now?"

128
00:05:41.978 --> 00:05:47.281
"We should find our suspects quickly and question them," Henry said.

129
00:05:48.282 --> 00:05:51.304
Before his friends could answer, the PA system came on.

130
00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:56.580
"I hope you're all enjoying Belltown Arts Day," the mayor's voice said.

131
00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:01.428
"Everyone is very excited to find out the winners of our yearly art show.

132
00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.456
The official judging will begin in an hour and a half."
